-controlled code points for validation and normalization."}, {"step": 8, "file": "src-vul/libidn2/lib/idna.c", "function": "_idn2_label_test", "line": 120, "var": "label", "code": "if (what & TEST_DISALLOWED) { for (i = 0; i < llen; i++) if (_idn2_disallowed_p (label[i])) ... }", "note": "The decoded label is checked against IDNA rules before conversion proceeds."}, {"step": 9, "file": "src-vul/libidn2/lib/idna.c", "function": "_idn2_label_test", "line": 151, "var": "label", "code": "if (what & TEST_BIDI) { int rc = _idn2_bidi (label, llen); if (rc != IDN2_OK) return rc; }", "note": "Bidirectional-text validation is applied to the same decoded label as part of the conversion pipeline."}, {"step": 10, "file": "src-vul/libidn2/lib/idna.c", "function": "_idn2_u8_to_u32_nfc", "line": 92, "var": "tmp", "code": "uint32_t *tmp = u32_normalize (UNINORM_NFC, p, plen, NULL, &tmplen);", "note": "If the label is not already NFC, it is normalized into a new UTF-32 buffer before punycode encoding."}, {"step": 11, "file": "src-vul/libpsl/src/psl.c", "function": "psl_idna_toASCII", "line": 780, "var": "lookupname", "code": "if (domain_to_punycode(utf8, lookupname, sizeof(lookupname)) == 0) { ... }", "note": "The converted label is copied into a fixed-size stack buffer for punycode output; an oversized or malformed conversion can overflow this sink in the vulnerable build."}]